<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company complies with the requirement of the ASC 340-10-S99-1 and SEC Staff Accounting Bulletin (&ldquo;SAB&rdquo;) Topic 5A &mdash;
&ldquo;Expenses of Offering.&rdquo; Deferred offering costs consist of underwriting, legal, and other expenses incurred
through the balance sheet date that are directly related to the Company&rsquo;s intended follow-up offering. Deferred offering
costs will be charged to shareholders&rsquo; equity upon the completion of the follow-up offering. Should the follow-up offering prove
to be unsuccessful, these deferred costs, as well as additional expenses to be incurred, will be charged to operations. As of June 30,
2023, the Company capitalized $0.4 million of deferred offering costs.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

